WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:05.729
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
The Flash introduced Robbie Amell as Ronnie

00:00:05.729 --> 00:00:11.400
Raymond and the Kyle Nimbus character from
the comics.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.480
He was The Mist on the show, but in the comics
he was a little different so I’ll explain

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.480
that during my Top 5 moments.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:21.730
It was definitely my favorite episode so far,
so careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:22.730
it.

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:26.000
Starting with Number 5 - Meet Kyle Nimbus
aka The Mist

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.930
In the comics, Kyle Nimbus was from the starman
comics and was known as the son of The Mist.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.260
So that was a minor change.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:35.920
I also think it’s cool they did a character
from outside the flash comics.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:37.739
Like they pulled in other titles.

00:00:37.739 --> 00:00:43.160
It means that we could see characters from
all over the dc universe in the future.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:48.170
On the show I really appreciated the way they
presented his powers using science.

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:51.410
I feel like The Flash as a show has been winning
at Science.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:56.480
Maybe it’s just because I love hard science
fiction so much, but magic or super powers

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:08.070
are just science we haven’t learned to understand
yet.

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:09.080
Science will always win.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:13.400
Remember that idea, it’s important to understanding
what’s going on with Harrison Wells and

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.570
the great villain arc this season.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:17.400
Science will always win over raw muscle.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.060
That’s why people are always able to outsmart
Superman.

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:22.930
Although technically he’s a pretty good
scientist to.

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:26.130
The movies and the tv shows have just done
a very poor job of portraying that.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:31.360
Number 4 - The Particle Accelerator Becomes
a Metahuman Prison

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:36.320
Crazy thought here, Harrison Wells talked
about finding a way to take away their powers.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:39.470
Imagine by the end of the season they capture
a bunch of metahumans.

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:43.750
What if Harrison wants to use their powers
to fuel some big catastrophe.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:47.380
Or even just steal the energy to make himself
more powerfull.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:58.670
If he really is Eobard Thawne from the comics,
he already has the Negative Speed Force.

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:03.390
Regardless of what their long term plan is
for all the future inmates, it looks badass

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:04.390
from a visual perspective.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.850
It’s like Cerebro on Steroids.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.440
It’s a super collider like the one at CERN.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:12.349
So that’s why it looks like the Large Hadron
Collider.

00:02:12.349 --> 00:02:15.849
Their design was inspired by the large hadron
collider.

00:02:15.849 --> 00:02:31.720
If you look at it in real life it’s like
a masterpiece of science and engineering artwork.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.940
I think they said that the Star Labs collider
is non functioning.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:38.870
But the parts that still do work are what
they’re using to power the prison cells.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:41.590
But as a facility it’s massive.

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:44.099
It’s like the size of the Triskelion in
the Marvel Universe.

00:02:44.099 --> 00:02:46.349
And it’s all underground.

00:02:46.349 --> 00:02:49.170
Number 3 - Grant Gustin and John Wesley Shipp

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.689
Just in general all the Original Flash scenes
were great.

00:02:51.689 --> 00:02:56.549
When I’m watching the show I just call the
scenes he gets with Grant Gustin Flash Squared

00:02:56.549 --> 00:02:57.549
moments.

00:02:57.549 --> 00:03:00.200
His dad’s character is the moral lightning
rod of the show.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.659
Just to make a flash joke.

00:03:01.659 --> 00:03:06.060
So he gets to be the wise master teaching
Grant Gustin what it means to be a hero without

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:08.409
it turning into a classroom learning situation.

00:03:08.409 --> 00:03:10.120
He’s Barry’s Jonathan Kent.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:16.019
Jonathan is the moral core of superman so
when you think of John Wesley Shipp just think

00:03:16.019 --> 00:03:17.450
of him like that.

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:22.900
He shares the job a little with Detective
West, a lot of what he said was pretty obvious

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:28.459
foreshadowing like “you can’t save everyone”
so when you look at his dad’s line “you

00:03:28.459 --> 00:03:29.560
ran to your mother”.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:31.529
You can imagine what they’re teasing.

00:03:31.529 --> 00:03:36.180
Barry has to learn that even if he can run
fast enough to save everyone, he still can’t

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.610
save everyone.

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:40.900
Now twist that on it’s head with Harrison
Well’s line “You’d be surprised what

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:42.090
you can live with”.

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:47.090
Using Barry as context, he’ll learn to live
with his mother’s death eventually.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:50.019
Even with all of his powers.

00:03:50.019 --> 00:03:53.260
Number 2 - Harrison Wells Flashback

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:56.560
After the flashback that line “you’d be
surprised at what you can live with” is

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:58.150
so much more important.

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:04.010
He clearly precipitated the particle accelerator
explosion to cause the tear in spacetime facilitating

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.790
Barry’s speed force accident.

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:10.249
There is a predestination paradox at play
that comic book readers will know all about.

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:15.529
So if you have read Flash Rebirth, just please
use spoiler tags.

00:04:15.529 --> 00:04:20.389
But think of what Oliver Queen told Barry
in episode 1 “I think that Lightning Chose

00:04:20.389 --> 00:04:21.389
You”.

00:04:21.389 --> 00:04:22.389
That means more than you think it means.

00:04:22.389 --> 00:04:23.389
They’ll explain that by the end of season
1.

00:04:23.389 --> 00:04:26.190
It doesn’t mean that Harrison Wells is the
lightning, he didn’t directly give Barry

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:27.190
his powers.

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:29.990
He just knew what needed to happen in order
for him to get the powers.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:32.940
So he helped facilitate it with the explosion.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:38.040
It makes you wonder how long had Wells been
working at Star Labs?

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:41.780
I wouldn’t be surprised if it turned out
he mysteriously started working there right

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:43.800
after Barry’s Mother was Murdered.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:47.729
Number 1 - Meet Ronnie Raymond aka Firestorm

